#
# Fail-witness for the no-duplicate ban on SEMANTIC-TOPOLOGY (charter Hard Rule 10,
# ex:saNoRemintSemanticTopologyTerms): a fixture that RE-MINTS gmeow:TopologyClaim as
# rdfs:isDefinedBy the preference slice — the AC7 no-duplication violation (Principle 16). The
# preference sheaf apparatus is its own twin (gmeow:ComparisonCompilation / gmeow:ConsensusSection
# / gmeow:DisagreementObstruction) and reuses the sibling by-reference only. Unioned with the
# module by the gmeow:saFailWitness teeth check, it makes the ∃-redeclared-term ASK HOLD, proving
# the mustNot ban has teeth. The module must never carry this triple.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

gmeow:TopologyClaim rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/preference> .
